# Backend

- Layering: entry point (controller / Livewire / Filament action) -> validate -> authorise (Policy) -> Service -> Eloquent -> MySQL.
- Database operations and business rules belong in app/Services. Entry points stay thin.
- Multi-step writes use DB::transaction(); use lockForUpdate() for money, matric numbers and result publication.
- Authorise every action and every route that takes an id. Use visibleTo() scopes for staff lists.
- Payments: use only the PaymentGateway interface (Remita, Interswitch, Demo; no Paystack). Never trust redirects, callbacks or notification bodies; they only trigger a re-query. Check status/amount/currency/reference, settle idempotently in a transaction with lockForUpdate. Pending payments are polled and expire.
- Imports: validate every row, chunk commits (25 rows), be idempotent, guard Google Sheet fetches (host allow-list, size/time limits, no cross-host redirects).
- Email only through MailService (outbox + queue). Providers only through their interface/adapter.
- Schema changes only via new migrations; never edit an applied migration. Add indexes and foreign keys.
- Use $fillable allow-lists, bound parameters, enums for statuses/roles. Eager-load to avoid N+1.
- Write audit entries and enqueue emails inside the service that performs the action.
- Never log passwords, tokens, keys or provider secrets.
